## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical monocular 6-DoF pose estimator that handles symmetry, occlusion, and online adaptation in a real-world manufacturing setting. Emphasizes differentiable refinement, data strategies, and latency planning.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose estimation
- Differentiable rendering for pose refinement
- Symmetry handling and occlusion robustness
- Synthetic data + domain randomization
- Online adaptation with few-shot updates
- Real-time latency targets (embedded GPU)

## Code Example
```javascript
class PoseHead {
  constructor(featDim) {
    this.fcRot = linear(featDim, 4); // quaternion
    this.fcTrans = linear(featDim, 3);
  }
  forward(feat) {
    const q = normalize(this.fcRot(feat), 2);
    const t = this.fcTrans(feat);
    return { quat: q, trans: t };
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate symmetry handling for objects with known symmetry? 
- How would you mitigate catastrophic forgetting during online adaptation?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses handling of articulated, hinge-based objects in clutter, real-time constraints, and on-device adaptation with few shots.

## Key Concepts

- Articulated 6-DoF pose estimation for hinged objects
- Hinge-state (open/closed) inference
- Synthetic+real data with domain adaptation
- Few-shot on-device fine-tuning
- Real-time edge deployment considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pose error metric example (illustrative)
function poseError(est, gt) {
  // est/gt: {R: rotation matrix, t: translation vector}
  const rotError = rotationDistance(est.R, gt.R);
  const transError = vectorDistance(est.t, gt.t);
  return { rotError, transError };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you mitigate pose ambiguity from symmetric trays?
- How would you extend to add new hinge geometries online without retraining a large model?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design production-ready, on-device face verification systems with robust anti-spoofing capabilities under strict computational constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Edge-optimized inference architectures
- 3D head pose estimation from facial landmarks
- Temporal liveness detection for spoof resistance
- Parameter-efficient 5-shot adaptation via adapter layers
- Hybrid synthetic-to-real data generation strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: unified inference pipeline
function processFrame(frame) {
  const backbone = extractFeatures(frame);
  const detection = faceDetectionHead(backbone);
  const liveness = temporalLivenessHead(backbone);
  return { detection, liveness };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CV design with 3D reconstruction, uncertainty, and fast on-device adaptation, crucial for tool manipulation in cluttered spaces.

## Key Concepts
- 3D pose + mesh prediction from monocular input
- Uncertainty estimation and active adaptation
- Edge-efficient architectures and losses for consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
function loss(params){
  const L2 = reprojLoss(params);
  const Lpose = poseLoss(params);
  const Lmesh = meshLoss(params);
  const Lreg = temporalEdgeReg(params);
  return L2 + Lpose + Lmesh + Lreg;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you calibrate uncertainty for active-learning? 
- What would you change for multiple simultaneous tools?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates robust multi-hand 3D pose with fine-grained articulation under occlusion, plus on-device adaptation for real-world diversity.

## Key Concepts
- 3D hand pose (finger joints), hand mesh (MANO)
- Temporal tracking and occlusion handling
- On-device few-shot adaptation and edge latency

## Code Example
```javascript
function totalLoss(key3d, pred3d, mesh3d, predMesh3d, tio, contactPred, contactGT){
  const lKey = mse(key3d, pred3d);
  const lMesh = l2(mesh3d, predMesh3d);
  const lTemp = mse(pred3d, tio);
  const lContact = crossEntropy(contactGT, contactPred);
  return 0.4*lKey + 0.3*lMesh + 0.2*lTemp + 0.1*lContact;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate hand-object contact reliability in clutter?
- What ablations would you run to isolate the impact of articulation accuracy vs. contact estimation?
